  "worked_solution": "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{-1}7\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =14 \\\\ 7{\\int }_{5}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =14 \\\\ -7{\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =14 \\\\ {\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-4}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
